From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ole32: Embed a file without an OLE server as a Package in OleCreateFromFileEx.

AI-assisted (Claude), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted
upstream.
Contributed by krokosik (Autodesk-Inventor-for-Linux issue #10, winum PR
#1), written with Claude and cross-reviewed by Codex
(docs/wine-repro/cross-review-2026-11-12-inventor-reference-model.md).

Windows (measured, Windows 10 22H2, 2026-11-11): OleCreateFromFileEx on a
file whose class is not an OLE embedding server (.htm, .txt, an unknown
extension) succeeds and creates a Package: class
{0003000C-0000-0000-C000-000000000046}, user type "Package", storage with
\1CompObj and \1Ole10Native (label, source path, temp path, contents, and
the three paths again in UTF-16). This also holds for .htm, although MSHTML
there can load the file; no class involved is marked Insertable.

Wine bound the file moniker to IDataObject and failed (MSHTML:
IPersistFile::Load not implemented; other types MK_E_INVALIDEXTENSION).
Autodesk Inventor 2027 embeds its import report (.htm) this way; Import CAD
with Reference Model ended with "Could not Insert Object".

Limited to files whose class has no Insertable key under its CLSID;
such a class keeps the existing path. For a package, OLERENDER_FORMAT
stores no cache either (measured), so it is accepted without one (FIXME
kept). The \1CompObj user type is "OLE Package" as
measured; Windows also writes the ProgID "Package", which Wine's
WriteFmtUserTypeStg leaves out when the class has none registered.

v2 (2026-11-11, after cross review): a file is packaged only when it is
not a compound file and its class has no Insertable key under its CLSID or
its ProgID; the last error is saved before WARN; files over 2 GB and paths
of MAX_PATH or more are refused instead of being cut short (the package
format holds MAX_PATH paths).

v3 (2026-11-12, after cross review by Codex; measured with pkgprobe,
Windows 10 22H2 x64 and x86, docs/wine-repro/ole32-createfromfile-html):
only an Insertable key under the CLSID keeps the class path - a ProgID
marked Insertable still gives a Package on Windows, so that check is gone.
A file that cannot be opened (missing, a directory, opened by another
handle without sharing) and a path of MAX_PATH or more return
STG_E_FILENOTFOUND as on Windows. The contents are copied in chunks
instead of being read into memory; size and read errors are reported
separately. Tests: the failures, an empty file, and the Insertable cases;
the extent of a Package follows its label (width grows with the name,
height does not, every aspect the same). The test registers its class in
HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT where allowed, else under HKCU (Wine's HKCR does not show
HKCU-only classes to RegQueryValueW). Temporary names carry the process id.

v4 (2026-11-12, after the second review; measured with pkgprobe on
Windows 10 22H2, x64 and x86): the writer no longer refuses a path whose
ANSI form is longer than MAX_PATH - what Windows does with such a path
(a multibyte code page) is not measured; the packager now reads such a
package through its UTF-16 name instead. Tests: the registered class
names are unique per process; the Package's extent and its drawing on a
scaled, offset DC; loading with a temporary directory near the limit (fits, fits
only without a " (2)", fits neither). All passed on Windows 10 x86_64 and
i686.

v5 (2026-11-12, after the third review): exact extents are checked only
in the configurations measured (96 dpi, 32x32 icons, Segoe UI icon title
font 15 or 25 pixels high), elsewhere skipped; that the width follows the
label and the height does not is checked always. The temporary directory
limit is also checked for a Package without the UTF-16 names (ANSI only),
which Windows loads with the same limit (pkgprobe part O, x64 and x86).
Temporary directory names carry the tick count as well. Passed on Windows
10 x86_64 and i686.

--- a/dlls/ole32/ole2.c
+++ b/dlls/ole32/ole2.c
@@ -3010,6 +3010,121 @@
     return hr;
 }
 
+/* {0003000C-0000-0000-C000-000000000046}, the OLE 1 Package object (packager.dll) */
+static const CLSID clsid_package = {0x0003000c, 0, 0, {0xc0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0x46}};
+
+/* Whether a file is embedded by its own class: compound files, and files whose
+ * class is marked Insertable under its CLSID (an Insertable key under the
+ * ProgID alone still gives a Package, as on Windows). */
+static BOOL embed_by_class(const OLECHAR *filename)
+{
+    CLSID clsid;
+    HKEY key;
+
+    if (StgIsStorageFile( filename ) == S_OK) return TRUE;
+    if (FAILED(GetClassFile( filename, &clsid ))) return FALSE;
+    if (COM_OpenKeyForCLSID( &clsid, L"Insertable", KEY_READ, &key ) != S_OK) return FALSE;
+    RegCloseKey( key );
+    return TRUE;
+}
+
+static HRESULT write_counted( IStream *stm, const void *data, DWORD len, DWORD count )
+{
+    HRESULT hr = IStream_Write( stm, &count, sizeof(count), NULL );
+    if (SUCCEEDED(hr)) hr = IStream_Write( stm, data, len, NULL );
+    return hr;
+}
+
+/* Wraps a file without an OLE server in a Package: the \1Ole10Native stream
+ * holds the file's name, path and contents. */
+static HRESULT create_package( const OLECHAR *filename, IStorage *stg )
+{
+    static const WORD type = 2, unknown[2] = { 0, 3 };
+    static WCHAR user_type[] = L"OLE Package";
+    const WCHAR *label = wcsrchr( filename, '\\' ) ? wcsrchr( filename, '\\' ) + 1 : filename;
+    DWORD label_len = wcslen( label ), path_len = wcslen( filename );
+    DWORD labela_len, patha_len, size, total, read;
+    LARGE_INTEGER filesize;
+    char *labela = NULL, *patha = NULL;
+    BYTE buf[0x4000];
+    IStream *stm;
+    HANDLE file;
+    HRESULT hr;
+
+    /* Windows answers a path of MAX_PATH or more, like any file it cannot
+     * open, with STG_E_FILENOTFOUND (measured) */
+    if (path_len >= MAX_PATH) return STG_E_FILENOTFOUND;
+    patha_len = WideCharToMultiByte( CP_ACP, 0, filename, -1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL );
+    labela_len = WideCharToMultiByte( CP_ACP, 0, label, -1, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL );
+
+    file = CreateFileW( filename, GENERIC_READ, FILE_SHARE_READ | FILE_SHARE_WRITE, NULL, OPEN_EXISTING, 0, NULL );
+    if (file == INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE)
+    {
+        WARN( "cannot open %s: %lu\n", debugstr_w(filename), GetLastError() );
+        return STG_E_FILENOTFOUND;
+    }
+    if (!GetFileSizeEx( file, &filesize ))
+    {
+        hr = HRESULT_FROM_WIN32( GetLastError() );
+        CloseHandle( file );
+        return hr;
+    }
+    /* the stream's sizes are DWORDs */
+    if (filesize.QuadPart > 0x7fff0000)
+    {
+        CloseHandle( file );
+        return STG_E_MEDIUMFULL;
+    }
+    size = filesize.u.LowPart;
+
+    if (!(labela = malloc( labela_len )) || !(patha = malloc( patha_len )))
+    {
+        hr = E_OUTOFMEMORY;
+        goto done;
+    }
+    WideCharToMultiByte( CP_ACP, 0, label, -1, labela, labela_len, NULL, NULL );
+    WideCharToMultiByte( CP_ACP, 0, filename, -1, patha, patha_len, NULL, NULL );
+
+    hr = IStorage_CreateStream( stg, L"\1Ole10Native", STGM_CREATE | STGM_WRITE | STGM_SHARE_EXCLUSIVE, 0, 0, &stm );
+    if (FAILED(hr)) goto done;
+
+    total = sizeof(type) + labela_len + patha_len + sizeof(unknown) + 4 + patha_len + 4 + size
+            + 4 + path_len * sizeof(WCHAR) + 4 + label_len * sizeof(WCHAR) + 4 + path_len * sizeof(WCHAR);
+    hr = IStream_Write( stm, &total, sizeof(total), NULL );
+    if (SUCCEEDED(hr)) hr = IStream_Write( stm, &type, sizeof(type), NULL );
+    if (SUCCEEDED(hr)) hr = IStream_Write( stm, labela, labela_len, NULL );
+    if (SUCCEEDED(hr)) hr = IStream_Write( stm, patha, patha_len, NULL );
+    if (SUCCEEDED(hr)) hr = IStream_Write( stm, unknown, sizeof(unknown), NULL );
+    if (SUCCEEDED(hr)) hr = write_counted( stm, patha, patha_len, patha_len );
+    if (SUCCEEDED(hr)) hr = IStream_Write( stm, &size, sizeof(size), NULL );
+    /* the contents, as many bytes as counted above */
+    while (SUCCEEDED(hr) && size)
+    {
+        if (!ReadFile( file, buf, min( size, sizeof(buf) ), &read, NULL ))
+            hr = HRESULT_FROM_WIN32( GetLastError() );
+        else if (!read)
+            hr = STG_E_READFAULT; /* the file shrank while it was copied */
+        else
+        {
+            hr = IStream_Write( stm, buf, read, NULL );
+            size -= read;
+        }
+    }
+    if (SUCCEEDED(hr)) hr = write_counted( stm, filename, path_len * sizeof(WCHAR), path_len );
+    if (SUCCEEDED(hr)) hr = write_counted( stm, label, label_len * sizeof(WCHAR), label_len );
+    if (SUCCEEDED(hr)) hr = write_counted( stm, filename, path_len * sizeof(WCHAR), path_len );
+    IStream_Release( stm );
+
+    if (SUCCEEDED(hr)) hr = WriteClassStg( stg, &clsid_package );
+    if (SUCCEEDED(hr)) hr = WriteFmtUserTypeStg( stg, 0, user_type );
+
+done:
+    CloseHandle( file );
+    free( labela );
+    free( patha );
+    return hr;
+}
+
 /******************************************************************************
  *              OleCreateFromFileEx        [OLE32.@]
  */
@@ -3030,6 +3145,23 @@
     for (i = 0; i < num_fmts; i++)
         TRACE("\t%ld: fmt %s adv flags %ld\n", i, debugstr_formatetc(fmts + i), adv_flags[i]);
 
+    /* Files whose class is not an OLE embedding server (also .htm, .txt or an
+     * unknown extension) are embedded as a Package, like Windows does. */
+    if (!embed_by_class( filename ))
+    {
+        if (renderopt == OLERENDER_FORMAT) FIXME( "caching formats of a package is not supported\n" );
+        hr = create_package( filename, stg );
+        if (SUCCEEDED(hr)) hr = OleLoad( stg, &IID_IUnknown, client_site, (void**)&unk );
+        if (FAILED(hr))
+        {
+            WARN( "embedding %s as a package failed: %#lx\n", debugstr_w(filename), hr );
+            return hr;
+        }
+        hr = IUnknown_QueryInterface( unk, iid, obj );
+        IUnknown_Release( unk );
+        return hr;
+    }
+
     hr = CreateFileMoniker( filename, &mon );
     if (FAILED(hr)) return hr;
 
--- a/dlls/ole32/tests/ole2.c
+++ b/dlls/ole32/tests/ole2.c
@@ -4618,6 +4618,510 @@
     ReleaseStgMedium( NULL );
 }
 
+static void test_OleCreateFromFile_package(void)
+{
+    static const CLSID clsid_package = {0x0003000c, 0, 0, {0xc0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0x46}};
+    static const char contents[] = "<html><body>package test</body></html>\r\n";
+    static const WCHAR *const exts[] = { L".htm", L".wtst" };
+    WCHAR path[MAX_PATH], name[MAX_PATH];
+    char buf[1024];
+    IStorage *stg;
+    IStream *stm;
+    IUnknown *obj;
+    CLSID clsid;
+    HANDLE file;
+    DWORD written;
+    ULONG read;
+    HRESULT hr;
+    BOOL found;
+    int i;
+    ULONG j;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(exts); i++)
+    {
+        winetest_push_context("%s", wine_dbgstr_w(exts[i]));
+
+        GetTempPathW(ARRAY_SIZE(path), path);
+        swprintf(name, ARRAY_SIZE(name), L"winetest_olecff%lu%s", GetCurrentProcessId(), exts[i]);
+        lstrcatW(path, name);
+        file = CreateFileW(path, GENERIC_WRITE, 0, NULL, CREATE_ALWAYS, 0, NULL);
+        ok(file != INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE, "CreateFile failed: %lu\n", GetLastError());
+        WriteFile(file, contents, sizeof(contents) - 1, &written, NULL);
+        CloseHandle(file);
+
+        hr = StgCreateDocfile(NULL, STGM_READWRITE | STGM_CREATE | STGM_SHARE_EXCLUSIVE | STGM_DELETEONRELEASE, 0, &stg);
+        ok(hr == S_OK, "StgCreateDocfile failed: %#lx\n", hr);
+
+        /* how Autodesk Inventor embeds its translation report */
+        obj = NULL;
+        hr = OleCreateFromFileEx(&CLSID_NULL, path, &IID_IUnknown, 0, OLERENDER_NONE, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL,
+                                 NULL, stg, (void **)&obj);
+        ok(hr == S_OK, "OleCreateFromFileEx failed: %#lx\n", hr);
+        ok(obj != NULL, "got NULL object\n");
+
+        hr = ReadClassStg(stg, &clsid);
+        ok(hr == S_OK, "ReadClassStg failed: %#lx\n", hr);
+        ok(IsEqualCLSID(&clsid, &clsid_package), "got class %s\n", wine_dbgstr_guid(&clsid));
+
+        hr = IStorage_OpenStream(stg, L"\1Ole10Native", NULL, STGM_READ | STGM_SHARE_EXCLUSIVE, 0, &stm);
+        ok(hr == S_OK, "OpenStream(\\1Ole10Native) failed: %#lx\n", hr);
+        if (hr == S_OK)
+        {
+            read = 0;
+            IStream_Read(stm, buf, sizeof(buf), &read);
+            found = FALSE;
+            for (j = 0; j + sizeof(contents) - 1 <= read; j++)
+                if (!memcmp(buf + j, contents, sizeof(contents) - 1)) found = TRUE;
+            ok(found, "file contents not in the package stream (%lu bytes)\n", read);
+            IStream_Release(stm);
+        }
+
+        if (obj) IUnknown_Release(obj);
+        IStorage_Release(stg);
+        DeleteFileW(path);
+        winetest_pop_context();
+    }
+}
+
+/* per process, so that concurrent test runs do not share registry keys */
+static WCHAR probe_ext[32], probe_progid[64], probe_clsid_key[64];
+
+/* HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT where it may be written, otherwise the user's classes
+ * (Windows refuses new HKCR keys to a standard user) */
+static HKEY classes_root;
+
+static void set_class_key(const WCHAR *key, const WCHAR *value)
+{
+    HKEY hkey;
+    LONG ret;
+
+    ret = RegCreateKeyExW(classes_root, key, 0, NULL, 0, KEY_WRITE, NULL, &hkey, NULL);
+    ok(!ret, "RegCreateKeyEx(%s) failed: %ld\n", wine_dbgstr_w(key), ret);
+    if (ret) return;
+    if (value) RegSetValueExW(hkey, NULL, 0, REG_SZ, (const BYTE *)value, (lstrlenW(value) + 1) * sizeof(WCHAR));
+    RegCloseKey(hkey);
+}
+
+static void delete_class_keys(void)
+{
+    RegDeleteTreeW(classes_root, probe_ext);
+    RegDeleteTreeW(classes_root, probe_progid);
+    RegDeleteTreeW(classes_root, probe_clsid_key);
+    RegDeleteKeyW(classes_root, probe_ext);
+    RegDeleteKeyW(classes_root, probe_progid);
+    RegDeleteKeyW(classes_root, probe_clsid_key);
+}
+
+static void open_classes_root(void)
+{
+    WCHAR guid[40];
+    GUID clsid;
+    HKEY hkey;
+
+    CoCreateGuid(&clsid);
+    StringFromGUID2(&clsid, guid, ARRAY_SIZE(guid));
+    swprintf(probe_ext, ARRAY_SIZE(probe_ext), L".wts%lu", GetCurrentProcessId());
+    swprintf(probe_progid, ARRAY_SIZE(probe_progid), L"WineTest.PkgProbe%lu", GetCurrentProcessId());
+    swprintf(probe_clsid_key, ARRAY_SIZE(probe_clsid_key), L"CLSID\\%s", guid);
+
+    if (!RegCreateKeyExW(HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT, probe_ext, 0, NULL, 0, KEY_WRITE, NULL, &hkey, NULL))
+    {
+        RegCloseKey(hkey);
+        RegDeleteKeyW(HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT, probe_ext);
+        RegOpenKeyExW(HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT, NULL, 0, KEY_ALL_ACCESS, &classes_root);
+        return;
+    }
+    RegCreateKeyExW(HKEY_CURRENT_USER, L"Software\\Classes", 0, NULL, 0, KEY_ALL_ACCESS, NULL, &classes_root, NULL);
+}
+
+static HRESULT create_from_file(const WCHAR *path, CLSID *clsid)
+{
+    IUnknown *obj = NULL;
+    IStorage *stg;
+    HRESULT hr;
+
+    hr = StgCreateDocfile(NULL, STGM_READWRITE | STGM_CREATE | STGM_SHARE_EXCLUSIVE | STGM_DELETEONRELEASE, 0, &stg);
+    ok(hr == S_OK, "StgCreateDocfile failed: %#lx\n", hr);
+    if (FAILED(hr)) return hr;
+    hr = OleCreateFromFile(&CLSID_NULL, path, &IID_IUnknown, OLERENDER_NONE, NULL, NULL, stg, (void **)&obj);
+    if (SUCCEEDED(hr)) ok(obj != NULL, "got NULL object\n");
+    else ok(!obj, "got object %p\n", obj);
+    memset(clsid, 0, sizeof(*clsid));
+    ReadClassStg(stg, clsid);
+    if (obj) IUnknown_Release(obj);
+    IStorage_Release(stg);
+    return hr;
+}
+
+/* what Windows 10 returned, measured with pkgprobe (docs/wine-repro) */
+static void test_OleCreateFromFile_package_errors(void)
+{
+    static const CLSID clsid_package = {0x0003000c, 0, 0, {0xc0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0x46}};
+    WCHAR dir[MAX_PATH], path[MAX_PATH + 100];
+    CLSID clsid;
+    HANDLE file;
+    HRESULT hr;
+    DWORD written;
+    int i;
+
+    GetTempPathW(ARRAY_SIZE(dir), dir);
+    swprintf(dir + lstrlenW(dir), MAX_PATH - lstrlenW(dir), L"winetest_olecff%lx%lx", GetCurrentProcessId(), GetTickCount());
+    ok(CreateDirectoryW(dir, NULL), "CreateDirectory failed: %lu\n", GetLastError());
+
+    swprintf(path, ARRAY_SIZE(path), L"%s\\missing.txt", dir);
+    hr = create_from_file(path, &clsid);
+    ok(hr == STG_E_FILENOTFOUND, "missing file: got %#lx\n", hr);
+
+    hr = create_from_file(dir, &clsid);
+    ok(hr == STG_E_FILENOTFOUND, "directory: got %#lx\n", hr);
+
+    swprintf(path, ARRAY_SIZE(path), L"%s\\locked.txt", dir);
+    file = CreateFileW(path, GENERIC_READ | GENERIC_WRITE, 0, NULL, CREATE_ALWAYS, 0, NULL);
+    ok(file != INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE, "CreateFile failed: %lu\n", GetLastError());
+    WriteFile(file, "locked\r\n", 8, &written, NULL);
+    hr = create_from_file(path, &clsid);
+    ok(hr == STG_E_FILENOTFOUND, "file opened without sharing: got %#lx\n", hr);
+    CloseHandle(file);
+    DeleteFileW(path);
+
+    swprintf(path, ARRAY_SIZE(path), L"%s\\empty.txt", dir);
+    file = CreateFileW(path, GENERIC_WRITE, 0, NULL, CREATE_ALWAYS, 0, NULL);
+    CloseHandle(file);
+    hr = create_from_file(path, &clsid);
+    ok(hr == S_OK, "empty file: got %#lx\n", hr);
+    ok(IsEqualCLSID(&clsid, &clsid_package), "empty file: got class %s\n", wine_dbgstr_guid(&clsid));
+    DeleteFileW(path);
+
+    swprintf(path, ARRAY_SIZE(path), L"%s\\", dir);
+    for (i = lstrlenW(path); i < MAX_PATH + 40; i++) path[i] = 'a';
+    lstrcpyW(path + i, L".txt");
+    hr = create_from_file(path, &clsid);
+    ok(hr == STG_E_FILENOTFOUND, "path of %u characters: got %#lx\n", lstrlenW(path), hr);
+
+    /* only an Insertable key under the CLSID keeps the class's own path */
+    open_classes_root();
+    swprintf(path, ARRAY_SIZE(path), L"%s\\probe%s", dir, probe_ext);
+    file = CreateFileW(path, GENERIC_WRITE, 0, NULL, CREATE_ALWAYS, 0, NULL);
+    WriteFile(file, "probe\r\n", 7, &written, NULL);
+    CloseHandle(file);
+    for (i = 0; i < 4; i++)
+    {
+        WCHAR key[128];
+
+        winetest_push_context("case %d", i);
+        delete_class_keys();
+        set_class_key(probe_ext, probe_progid);
+        set_class_key(probe_progid, L"Package probe");
+        if (i >= 1)
+        {
+            swprintf(key, ARRAY_SIZE(key), L"%s\\CLSID", probe_progid);
+            set_class_key(key, probe_clsid_key + 6);
+            set_class_key(probe_clsid_key, L"Package probe");
+            swprintf(key, ARRAY_SIZE(key), L"%s\\ProgID", probe_clsid_key);
+            set_class_key(key, probe_progid);
+        }
+        if (i == 2)
+        {
+            swprintf(key, ARRAY_SIZE(key), L"%s\\Insertable", probe_progid);
+            set_class_key(key, NULL);
+        }
+        if (i == 3)
+        {
+            swprintf(key, ARRAY_SIZE(key), L"%s\\Insertable", probe_clsid_key);
+            set_class_key(key, NULL);
+        }
+        hr = create_from_file(path, &clsid);
+        if (i < 3)
+        {
+            ok(hr == S_OK, "got %#lx\n", hr);
+            ok(IsEqualCLSID(&clsid, &clsid_package), "got class %s\n", wine_dbgstr_guid(&clsid));
+        }
+        else
+        {
+            ok(hr == REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG, "got %#lx\n", hr);
+            ok(IsEqualCLSID(&clsid, &CLSID_NULL), "got class %s\n", wine_dbgstr_guid(&clsid));
+        }
+        winetest_pop_context();
+    }
+    delete_class_keys();
+    RegCloseKey(classes_root);
+    DeleteFileW(path);
+    RemoveDirectoryW(dir);
+}
+
+static void draw_box(IViewObject2 *view, HDC dc, int window_org, RECT *box)
+{
+    RECTL bounds = { 10, 10, 60, 60 };
+    SIZE ext;
+    HRESULT hr;
+    int x, y;
+
+    PatBlt(dc, 0, 0, 400, 400, WHITENESS);
+    SetMapMode(dc, MM_ANISOTROPIC);
+    SetWindowExtEx(dc, 100, 100, NULL);
+    SetViewportExtEx(dc, 200, 200, NULL);
+    SetViewportOrgEx(dc, 50, 50, NULL);
+    SetWindowOrgEx(dc, window_org, window_org, NULL);
+    hr = IViewObject2_Draw(view, DVASPECT_CONTENT, -1, NULL, NULL, NULL, dc, &bounds, NULL, NULL, 0);
+    ok(hr == S_OK, "Draw failed: %#lx\n", hr);
+    GetWindowExtEx(dc, &ext);
+    ok(ext.cx == 100 && ext.cy == 100, "window extent changed to %ldx%ld\n", ext.cx, ext.cy);
+    ok(GetMapMode(dc) == MM_ANISOTROPIC, "map mode changed to %d\n", GetMapMode(dc));
+    SetMapMode(dc, MM_TEXT);
+    SetWindowOrgEx(dc, 0, 0, NULL);
+    SetViewportOrgEx(dc, 0, 0, NULL);
+    SetRect(box, 400, 400, -1, -1);
+    for (y = 0; y < 400; y++)
+        for (x = 0; x < 400; x++)
+            if (GetPixel(dc, x, y) != RGB(255, 255, 255))
+            {
+                if (x < box->left) box->left = x;
+                if (x > box->right) box->right = x;
+                if (y < box->top) box->top = y;
+                if (y > box->bottom) box->bottom = y;
+            }
+}
+
+/* a Package draws relative to its bounds as the DC maps them: moving the
+ * window origin by -20 logical units (40 device pixels at this scale)
+ * moves the drawing by 40 pixels, as on Windows 10; the DC's mapping is
+ * left as it was */
+static void check_package_draw(IViewObject2 *view)
+{
+    HBITMAP bmp, old;
+    HDC screen, dc;
+    RECT a, b;
+
+    screen = GetDC(NULL);
+    dc = CreateCompatibleDC(screen);
+    bmp = CreateCompatibleBitmap(screen, 400, 400);
+    ReleaseDC(NULL, screen);
+    old = SelectObject(dc, bmp);
+    draw_box(view, dc, 0, &a);
+    draw_box(view, dc, -20, &b);
+    ok(a.right >= 0 && b.right >= 0, "nothing drawn\n");
+    ok(b.left - a.left == 40 && b.top - a.top == 40 && b.right - a.right == 40 && b.bottom - a.bottom == 40,
+       "drawn at %ld,%ld-%ld,%ld and %ld,%ld-%ld,%ld\n", a.left, a.top, a.right, a.bottom, b.left, b.top, b.right, b.bottom);
+    SelectObject(dc, old);
+    DeleteObject(bmp);
+    DeleteDC(dc);
+}
